<!--
  modules/graph/pom.xml — Stage 2-f Task 4 module POM (Wave D)
  (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-stage2f-remaining-modules.md).

  STATUS: ADDITIVE and RUN BY HAND (mvn -pl modules/graph -am package from
  the reactor root, or mvn -f modules/graph/pom.xml package). Ant
  (modules/graph/build.xml + build.incl.xml) remains the real build; nothing
  here is wired into CMake or any release build yet.

  WHY THIS MODULE. Part of Wave D — four modules whose only unmigrated-wave
  dependency was gui (Wave C, now in the reactor). graph is the JGraphX-based
  diagram canvas xcos (Wave E) will sit on top of — 48 files across
  io/shape/utils/view/actions/event, the widest vendored-jar surface of this
  wave (four third-party jars against zero for history_browser and
  ui_data). NOTE: prebuildjava/build.xml:55 gates its own Ant target on
  `if="${build_xcos}"` — an Ant-level conditional, not a Wave-D dependency
  concern (this POM's own dependency set has nothing to do with xcos; see
  the ruled-out finding below). Maven has no equivalent per-module
  conditional; this reactor builds graph unconditionally, same as every
  other module.

  STEP 1 FINDINGS (./maven-module-deps.sh graph, 48 files):
    [1] imports (excluding graph's own packages):
      - com.mxgraph.* (canvas, io, model, shape, swing{,.handler,.util,
        .view}, util, view) — the JGraphX diagram library itself, this
        module's whole reason for existing. thirdparty/jgraphx-2.1.0.7.jar,
        below.
      - net.sourceforge.jeuclid.swing — MathML rendering inside graph labels.
        thirdparty/jeuclid-core-3.1.14.jar, below (same jar, same coordinate
        as modules/console/pom.xml and modules/helptools/pom.xml).
      - org.apache.batik.{anim.dom,bridge,dom,ext.awt,gvt,svggen,util} — SVG
        export of the diagram canvas. thirdparty/batik-all-1.17.jar, below
        (same jar, same coordinate as modules/helptools/pom.xml and
        modules/graphic_export/pom.xml).
      - org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath — label/GED text rendering, same single
        plain jar (no .fop.* classes touched) as modules/console/pom.xml,
        modules/gui/pom.xml. thirdparty/jlatexmath-1.0.7.jar, below.
      - org.scilab.modules.commons{,.gui}, gui.bridge.{checkboxmenuitem,
        menuitem}, gui.checkboxmenuitem, gui.events.callback, gui.menuitem,
        gui.messagebox, jvm, localization, types — five reactor
        dependencies, all below (all already migrated: Wave C for gui,
        earlier waves for the rest).
      - static org.scilab.modules.commons.OS — a static import of the same
        commons.OS class already covered by the commons dependency below.
      - org.w3c.dom, org.xml.sax — JDK (java.xml module), not a dependency.
    [2] reflection targets — RULED OUT: (none reported by the tool). Cross-
        checked with an independent `grep -rn 'Class\.forName\|loadClass('`
        sweep of all 48 files — zero hits, confirmed clean (see the
        modules/history_browser/pom.xml header for why this manual
        cross-check matters: the tool has a confirmed blind spot for
        reflection reached through one level of constant indirection, and
        this module gets the same independent check even though the
        tool itself reported nothing).
    [3] fully-qualified uses with no import: org.scilab.modules.xcos.io.
        codec.XcosObjectCodec — RULED OUT. The ONLY hit, in io/
        ScilabGraphCodec.java:109, is `@see org.scilab.modules.xcos.io.codec.
        XcosObjectCodec#afterDecode(...)` — a javadoc `@see` tag (confirmed
        by reading the file), not code. xcos is Wave E, not migrated —
        reproduced as an absence, the same class of non-finding as
        modules/gui/pom.xml's org.scilab.modules.ihm.* entries and Stage
        2-b's org.scilab.modules.core.Scilab. Every other name in this
        category (com.mxgraph.util.mxCellRenderer.CanvasFactory, the seven
        org.apache.batik.* classes, the four jlatexmath classes,
        commons.OS/gui.FindIconHelper/gui.ScilabLAF, the five gui.* classes,
        jvm.LoadClassPath, localization.Messages, and the nine
        org.scilab.modules.types.* classes) is already covered by the
        reactor/vendored dependencies below, nothing new.
  No manifest.class-path anywhere in build.xml (confirmed again in the
  Ant-built jar's manifest: Class-Path is the literal, never-interpolated
  string "${manifest.class-path}").

  JGRAPHX — com.mxgraph.{canvas,io,model,shape,swing{,.handler,.util,.view},
  util,view}.* across this module's io/shape/utils/view packages, the
  diagram-editing library graph exists to wrap. No confirmed Maven Central
  coordinate for the exact jar vendored here (thirdparty/jgraphx-2.1.0.7.jar;
  scilab-lib.properties.in:19 jgraphx.jar=@JGRAPHX@) — same standing as
  modules/gui/pom.xml's jhall entry: a LABEL, not a verified repository
  coordinate, but here corroborated directly from the jar's OWN manifest
  rather than only the package prefix (`unzip -p thirdparty/
  jgraphx-2.1.0.7.jar META-INF/MANIFEST.MF`): `Bundle-SymbolicName:
  com.mxgraph`, `Vendor: JGraph Ltd`, `Bundle-Version: 2.1.0.7` — groupId,
  and version below are taken directly from those three lines, artifactId
  from the jar's own vendored basename (matching the `jgraphx.jar` property
  name Ant itself uses). system scope means the coordinate is never actually
  resolved from a repository either way, so this is purely a documentation
  label with zero effect on the build.

  BATIK-ALL, JEUCLID-CORE, JLATEXMATH — all three cross-referenced from
  earlier modules rather than re-justified: batik-all's coordinate
  (org.apache.xmlgraphics:batik-all:1.17) is the same one used, and
  independently confirmed against the jar's own Maven-built manifest
  (Implementation-Title: org.apache.xmlgraphics:batik-all), in
  modules/helptools/pom.xml and modules/graphic_export/pom.xml; jeuclid-core
  is the same jar/coordinate as modules/console/pom.xml and
  modules/helptools/pom.xml; jlatexmath is the same single plain jar (no
  jlatexmath-fop — graph never touches org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath.fop.*,
  grep-confirmed zero hits) as modules/console/pom.xml, modules/helptools/
  pom.xml and modules/gui/pom.xml.

  IMPLEMENTATION-VERSION: present, frozen at the literal "00000000 0000",
  positioned between Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor exactly
  where Ant's own jar places it (confirmed against modules/graph/jar/
  org.scilab.modules.graph.jar's actual manifest before extraction: live
  value there was "20260719 1729", a DSTAMP/TSTAMP pair). Vendor string
  double-encoded ("Ã¨", bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — extracted, never retyped, same
  as every other module.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
    <artifactId>scilab-modules-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2027.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>graph</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <!-- build.xml:19 <property name="library.title" value="Graph drawing"/> -->
  <name>Graph drawing</name>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.commons.OS (also via a static import),
         commons.gui.{FindIconHelper, ScilabLAF}. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>commons</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.gui.{bridge.checkboxmenuitem.
         SwingScilabCheckBoxMenuItem, bridge.menuitem.SwingScilabMenuItem,
         checkboxmenuitem.{CheckBoxMenuItem,ScilabCheckBoxMenuItem},
         events.callback.{CallBack,CommonCallBack}, menuitem.{MenuItem,
         ScilabMenuItem}, messagebox.ScilabModalDialog}. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>gui</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.jvm.LoadClassPath. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>jvm</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages — the ordinary
         reactor-sibling idiom used across nearly every module. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>localization</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.types.{ScilabBoolean, ScilabDouble,
         ScilabInteger, ScilabIntegerTypeEnum, ScilabList, ScilabMList,
         ScilabString, ScilabTList, ScilabType} — the data model graph nodes
         carry. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>types</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- JGRAPHX — com.mxgraph.* across this module's io/shape/utils/view
         packages, the diagram-editing library this module wraps. LABEL, not
         a verified Maven Central coordinate — see this file's header
         comment for the jgraphx-2.1.0.7.jar manifest evidence
         (Bundle-SymbolicName: com.mxgraph, Vendor: JGraph Ltd,
         Bundle-Version: 2.1.0.7) the groupId/artifactId/version below were
         taken from directly. system scope means it is never actually
         resolved from a repository. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.mxgraph</groupId>
      <artifactId>jgraphx</artifactId>
      <version>2.1.0.7</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.apache.batik.{anim.dom.SAXSVGDocumentFactory, bridge.*,
         dom.GenericDOMImplementation, ext.awt.RenderingHintsKeyExt,
         gvt.GraphicsNode, svggen.*, util.XMLResourceDescriptor} — SVG export
         of the diagram canvas. SAME MECHANISM, SAME COORDINATE AS
         modules/helptools/pom.xml and modules/graphic_export/pom.xml
         (cross-referenced, not restated). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.xmlgraphics</groupId>
      <artifactId>batik-all</artifactId>
      <version>1.17</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- net.sourceforge.jeuclid.swing — MathML rendering inside graph
         labels. SAME JAR, SAME COORDINATE AS modules/console/pom.xml and
         modules/helptools/pom.xml (cross-referenced, not restated). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>net.sourceforge.jeuclid</groupId>
      <artifactId>jeuclid-core</artifactId>
      <version>3.1.14</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath.{ParseException, TeXConstants,
         TeXFormula, TeXIcon} — label/GED text rendering. Same single plain
         jar (no jlatexmath-fop; graph never touches the .fop.* classes) as
         modules/console/pom.xml, modules/helptools/pom.xml and
         modules/gui/pom.xml. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab.forge</groupId>
      <artifactId>jlatexmath</artifactId>
      <version>1.0.7</version>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- build.incl.xml:22 <property name="src.dir" location="src/java/"/>.
         Same source tree Ant compiles — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
         identical comment; nothing module-specific to add here. -->
    <sourceDirectory>src/java</sourceDirectory>

    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <archive>
            <!-- addMavenDescriptor=false and the Built-By entry are
                 inherited from the parent POM — not redeclared here. Same
                 manifestFile mechanism as modules/localization/pom.xml (see
                 that file's build comment for the full rationale).
                 MANIFEST-section.MF's bytes were EXTRACTED from the actual
                 Ant-built jar's META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (unzip -p
                 modules/graph/jar/org.scilab.modules.graph.jar
                 META-INF/MANIFEST.MF), never retyped: Specification-Vendor
                 and Implementation-Vendor both carry the double-mangled
                 "Ã¨" (bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
                 fuller comment for the mechanism. Implementation-Version is
                 present, frozen at the literal "00000000 0000", positioned
                 between Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor
                 exactly where Ant places it. -->
            <manifestFile>${project.basedir}/src/main/manifest/MANIFEST-section.MF</manifestFile>
          </archive>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
